WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:05.996
This is Inkraft: a benchmark
for Swiss social insurance law.

00:06.696 --> 00:11.815
How much is the minimum
full AHV pension per month?

00:11.815 --> 00:16.833
Ask an AI assistant,
and you might hear CHF 1,225.

00:17.383 --> 00:22.453
That was the law until the end of 2024.

00:22.453 --> 00:27.913
Since January 2025, it has been CHF 1,260.

00:28.613 --> 00:32.503
The answer is already written down,
on fedlex.

00:32.503 --> 00:36.600
And German,
French and Italian are equally binding.

00:36.600 --> 00:42.216
So each language gets its gold
answer from its own authentic text,

00:42.216 --> 00:44.343
not from a translation.

00:45.043 --> 00:49.672
Inkraft stores the rule
in force on 1 October 2026, and,

00:49.672 --> 00:54.466
for more than 50 amended provisions,
the rule it replaced.

00:54.466 --> 00:58.681
So we can tell a stale
answer from an invented one.

00:58.681 --> 01:03.558
And saying “I'm not sure”
is scored apart from being wrong.

01:04.258 --> 01:11.956
Inkraft has more than 300 core questions,
each in German, French and Italian.

01:11.956 --> 01:16.007
Every row links to the exact
version of the law,

01:16.007 --> 01:19.148
and a human checked a random sample.

01:19.848 --> 01:25.251
The result: where a rule changed
and Inkraft stores the old answer,

01:25.251 --> 01:31.696
Apertus is right less than one time
in ten, even with the date in the prompt.

01:31.696 --> 01:36.651
We also search the legal corpus
that Apertus was trained on:

01:36.651 --> 01:40.360
does it contain this paragraph,
and in which version?

01:41.060 --> 01:45.706
Before a model answers questions
from citizens, test it on the law.

01:46.506 --> 01:50.454
Inkraft.
Because the law is the answer key.
